|name2 = Colossal Benkei
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Colossal Benkei''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Like the other [[Ancient Heroes ULTRA SOULS (Gacha Event)|ULTRA SOULS]], Ushiwakamaru has significantly different stats between Normal (spammable) and Evolved Form (high performance), both of which can be used effectively depending on the situation.

==='''Normal Form'''===
In his first form, Ushiwakamaru has somewhat usable general stats. He is quite similar to [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], sharing identical range. While Ushiwakamaru has noticeably higher raw stats than Cameraman Cat, Cameraman Cat has more knockbacks, Survivor and lower speed, allowing her to be stacked much more easily. Considering the fact that + levels and Stat Talents can bridge the stat gap, Cameraman Cat is generally preferred for general usage. However, this shows that even in his first form, Ushiwakamaru can hold his own in mixed stages.

Of course, as the Ultra Souls' Legend Rare, the story completely changes when it comes to Angels. Combine Ushiwakamaru's [[Insane Damage]] and [[Resistance]] to Angels, and you have a monster of a spammable attacker that easily shreds any Angel he can reach. At Lv.30, he packs 16,150 DPS against Angels, around 10x the DPS of Cameraman Cat, and nearly double that of a first form [[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasa Jizo]]. He also packs an absurd 84,150 HP against Angels, almost as much as [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]], allowing him to easily bulk his way through [[Chickful A]], [[Angelic Sleipnir]] and [[Sunfish Jones]], giving him unusually high flexibility for a spammable attacker. At Lv.50, these stats become even more crazy with 25.6K anti-Angel DPS and 133K effective HP against them.

Especially when paired with Research combos, Ushiwakamaru's first form is already a potent Angel destroyer, being able to nearly solo many pure Angel stages like [[No Plan A (Deadly)|No Plan A]]. However, more ranged Angels like Angelic Sleipnir, Sunfish Jones and especially [[Winged Pigge]] may be tricky when paired with support from other Traits. In these scenarios, Ushiwakamaru's second form is usually better.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Colossal Benkai is a standard backline nuker similar to the likes of [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]]. This unit's goal is simple: to stand in the back and deal outrageously high burst damage that is guaranteed to eviscerate anything he comes into contact with. His base numbers are great! He outperforms many early-midgame units like [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]] and [[Miyamoku Musashi (Special Cat)|Miyamoku Musashi]], making him a good filler slot if there's even one problematic Angel enemy in a stage. However, as a specialist, he's a monster that deals a colossal 316,200 DPH to targets at Lv.30 (502,200 at Lv.50), translating to just around ~38,000 (~60,288) DPS.

This damage is usually enough to instantly eliminate most standard peons, like [[Angelic Gory]] and [[Heavenly Hippoe]], while heavily chunking midrange or backline supports such as Winged Pigge and Angelic Sleipnir. Colossal Benkei is generally preferred over Ushiwakamaru in oppressive stages where the latter's usage becomes difficult to fully utilize. For example: Winged Pigge's Omni Strike outranges Ushiwakamaru (340 > 250), heavily crippling his damage via Weaken. Many mixed stages tend to be similarly problematic for poor Ushiwakamaru, where certain peons or supports can get in the way of his target.

He has fantastic survivability with his [[Resistant|Resistance]] to Angels. At Lv.30, he has 637,500 effective HP, ballooning to 1,012,500 at Lv.50. This usually lets him outlast most targets that either outrange him or get the jump on him from a distance. Overall, a fantastic unit!

